\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RSUBNOUNtoNOUN1                 (* singular /onlyplur*)
< m1: SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
>

< m : NOUN{NOUNrec1}[head/SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
                    ]
>

     COMP 
         <
          C1: SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas * [count] <> []
            C11: NOT (OnlyPlur IN SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms)
            A11: NOUNrec1 := COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1);
                 NOUNrec1.numbers := [singular];
                 NOUNrec1.posscomas := [count]; 
                 (* oneigenlijke gebruik van inherent attribuut *)
            C12: OnlyPlur IN SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms
            A12: NOUNrec1 := COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1);
                 NOUNrec1.numbers := [plural]
          A1: @
         >

     DECOMP
     < 
      C1: SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas * [count] <> [] AND
          NOUNrec1 =  {req         : SUBNOUNrec1.req
                       env         : SUBNOUNrec1.env
                       plurforms   : SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms
                       genders     : SUBNOUNrec1.genders
                       affix       : SUBNOUNrec1.affix
                       class       : SUBNOUNrec1.class
                       deixis      : SUBNOUNrec1.deixis
                       aspect      : SUBNOUNrec1.aspect
                       retro       : SUBNOUNrec1.retro
                       affix       : SUBNOUNrec1.affix
                       sexes       : SUBNOUNrec1.sexes
                       subcs       : SUBNOUNrec1.subcs
                       temporal    : SUBNOUNrec1.temporal
                       animate     : SUBNOUNrec1.animate
                       human       : SUBNOUNrec1.human
                       thetanp     : SUBNOUNrec1.thetanp
                       nounpatterns: SUBNOUNrec1.nounpatterns
                       prepkey     : SUBNOUNrec1.prepkey
                       personal    : SUBNOUNrec1.personal
                       poss        : SUBNOUNrec1.poss
                      }
          C11: NOT OnlyPlur IN SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms AND
               singular IN NOUNrec1.numbers  AND
               NOUNrec1.posscomas = [count]
          A11: @ 
          C12: OnlyPlur IN SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms AND
               plural IN NOUNrec1.numbers 
          A12: @ 
       A1: @
 
     >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] SUBNOUNtoNOUN1
\item[* relevant examples:] garden, table, book, bloke, toy
\item[* language:]  English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CNformation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class)
\item[* date of creation:] 12-FEB-1988 11:52:44  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Assigning singular number to count nouns.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) cf. document
"De vertaling van getal" (doc. nr.  )
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item

Onlyplurals are accepted both by this rule and by Rsubnountonoun2. 
That is: {\em scissors } $\rightarrow$ {\em een schaar}, 
but also: {\em scissors} $\rightarrow$ {\em scharen}. 
\item
There may be examples where in 
generation there is no singular count noun available
where this is incorrect. 

\item
To be checked: gaat scissors in combinatie met een numeral ook met deze regel??
\item
In its present form the rule assigns to an inherent attribute of NOUNrec1.
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}
\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RSUBNOUNtoNOUN2    (* count plural; mass  cf. RSUBNOUNTONOUN3 *)
< m1: SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
>

< m : NOUN{NOUNrec1}[head/SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
                    ]
>

   PARAMETERS
      <
       numberpar:numbertype
      >


     COMP  
     < 
      C1: true

        C12: numberpar = singular AND
             (SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms * [OnlyPlur] <> [] )
                                                 (* funds *) OR
             (SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas  = [count])
        A12: NOUNrec1 := COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1);
             NOUNrec1.numbers := [plural];
        C13: numberpar = plural AND
             count IN SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas (* book *) AND
             SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms * [NoPlur] = [] 
        A13: NOUNrec1 := COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1);
             NOUNrec1.numbers := [plural];
      A1: @
     >

     DECOMP
     < 
      C1: NOUNrec1 = COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1)
        C13: plural IN NOUNrec1.numbers  AND
             count IN SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas (* book *) AND
             SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms * [NoPlur] = [] 
        A13: numberpar := plural;
      A1: @
     >
&

\end{verbatim}
