\begin{description}
\item[* name:] SUBNOUNtoNOUN2
\item[* relevant examples:] shoes, brains, tables, gardens
\item[* language:]  English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule)
\item[* subgrammar:] CNformation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) 
\item[* date of creation:] 13-FEB-1988 09:18:50  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] 
Assigning plural number to nouns 
that can occur as plural nouns
NB. Assigning singular number to mass nouns is taken over by RSUBNOUNTONOUN3
(21-04-90; FJ)
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item parameter function:\\
The parameter stores whether the plural or singular (sub)rule was applied.
Thus it can be prohibited 
that nouns which are both count and mass, may incorrectly yield a 
double translation. E.g. mass NP {\em komkommer} -> {\em cucumber}, {\em 
cucumbers}. 
\\
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RSUBNOUNtoNOUN3   (* mass singular *)
< m1: SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
>

< m : NOUN{NOUNrec1}[head/SUBNOUN{SUBNOUNrec1}[mu1]
                    ]
>

   PARAMETERS
      <
       numberpar:numbertype
      >

     COMP  
     < 
      C1: true 
        C11: numberpar = singular AND
             SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas * [mass] <> [] (* milk, cheese *) AND
             SUBNOUNrec1.plurforms * [OnlyPlur] = [] 
        A11: @ 
        C14: numberpar = plural AND
             SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas  = [mass] 
        A14: @
      A1: NOUNrec1 := COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1);
          NOUNrec1.numbers := [singular];
          NOUNrec1.posscomas := [mass]; 
          (*  is wijziging van  inhgerent attribuut;
              ipv posscomas zou op dit niveau actcomas verdedigbaar zijn;
              zonder deze reductie wordt bijv. 'forel" ook in 'a trout'
              vertaald *)
     >

     DECOMP
     < 
      C1: SUBNOUNrec1.posscomas * [mass] <> [] AND
          NOUNrec1 = COPYT_SUBNOUNtoNOUN(SUBNOUNrec1) AND
          singular IN NOUNrec1.numbers 
      A1: numberpar := singular;
     >
&

\end{verbatim}
