\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:]
Makes a CN (mass) out of an EN ('number' is determined in the rule 
SUBNOUNtoNOUN).
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:] 
Having three EN-keys in the lexicon, with the following attribute-values:
\begin{enumerate}
\item  posscomas: count\\
   number:    singular
\item posscomas: count\\
   number:    plural
\item posscomas: mass\\
  number:    singular
\end{enumerate}
